<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!-- ============================================================================================
     macOS CloudKit-enabled entitlements (Phase 7B) — READY TO ACTIVATE, NOT the default.

     The Mac default (`PersonalOpsAgentMac.entitlements`) plus the CloudKit + push entitlements
     SwiftData needs to mirror the store into the user's private iCloud database. Kept separate on
     purpose: provisioning a CloudKit container requires a PAID Apple Developer Program membership
     ($99/yr); a free Apple ID cannot sign an app declaring these keys. The whole project defaults
     to free-tier signing, so the default build must NOT declare CloudKit.

     The container id `iCloud.com.rajatarora.PersonalOpsAgent` is IDENTICAL to iOS's — that is the
     point: both the iPhone and this Mac mirror the SAME private database, which is what makes
     iPhone↔Mac sync work (Phase 7A handoff #1).

     To ACTIVATE sync on the Mac (after enrolling in the paid program and creating the container —
     see docs/CLOUDKIT_SETUP.md), do ONE of:
       (a) In Xcode, select the PersonalOpsAgentMac target → Signing & Capabilities → + Capability →
           iCloud → check "CloudKit" and add the container `iCloud.com.rajatarora.PersonalOpsAgent`.
       (b) Point the Mac target's `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS` at this file (Debug + Release):
           `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = App/PersonalOpsAgentMac.CloudKit.entitlements`.
     Then set `CLOUDKIT_SYNC_ENABLED=true` in `Secrets/Config.local` and run on the signed Mac.
     ============================================================================================ -->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.rajatarora.PersonalOpsAgent</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.com.rajatarora.PersonalOpsAgent</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudKit</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Push entitlement drives CloudKit's near-real-time sync notifications. On a paid account
	     Xcode/automatic-signing provisions this; change to `production` for a release build. -->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
